t the essentials right without pushing past our $150 price ceiling. At $129.99, they offer impressive ANC, a comfortable fit, and plenty of features for the money. In our testing, they reduced outside noise by an average of 84%, making them a strong choice for commuting, traveling, or working in a busy office.</p></div><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>Battery life is another big reason we recommend them. The Space 2 lasted 53 hours and 21 minutes with ANC enabled in our testing, so you won’t need to charge them very often. The sound benefits from some adjustments in the companion app, but that’s a reasonable tradeoff at this price.</p> </div><div class="e_e"><div class="e_y8"><div class="e_D8"><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>The Space 2 show just how much noise canceling headphones have improved at this price. Our testing found that their ANC reduces ambient noise by an average of 84%, which is particularly useful when you want to concentrate without turning up the volume. We also appreciate the comfortable design, especially for longer listening sessions.</p></div><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>The companion app lets you customize the experience, and we’d recommend spending a few minutes adjusting the EQ. The default sound isn’t the main reason to buy these headphones, but the available adjustments help make them more versatile.</p> </div><div class="e_e e_lf"><q>With 84% average noise reduction and more than 53 hours of tested ANC-on battery life, the Space 2 deliver where budget headphones need to.</q></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <p>At $129.99 MSRP, the Space 2 offer an excellent combination of ANC, battery life, comfort, and features. They’re the headphones we’d recommend first to most people shopping under $150.</p> </div><div class="e_rF e_f e_e e_c7"><button type="button" class="e_f7" aria-label="Play video"><span class="e_g7"></span></button></div></div></div><button type="button" class="e_C8 e_T1 e_31 e_Z1 e_V1">Read more</button></div></div><span class="e_C6"><div class="e_D6"