d: </span>Mic on calls</li></ul><div class="e_lib e_qj"><span id=":R7eqm3m7r6d6:" class="e_mib">Did this help you decide?</span><span class="e_nib" role="group" aria-labelledby=":R7eqm3m7r6d6:"><button type="button" class="e_oib">Yes</button><button type="button" class="e_oib">No</button></span><span class="e_rib">Be the first to say</span><div class="e_vib"></div><button type="button" class="e_5hb">Ask Matias Cerpa</button></div><div id=":R1eqm3m7r6d6:" class="e_9hb e_Vj" hidden=""><ul class="e_-hb"><li><button type="button" class="e_6hb">Still using them every day?</button></li><li><button type="button" class="e_6hb">Comfortable with glasses on?</button></li><li><button type="button" class="e_6hb">How have the ear pads and headband held up?</button></li></ul><div class="e_jib"></div></div></div></article></div></section></div></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <hr/> <p>You don’t need to spend a fortune to get effective noise canceling, and the <a href="https://www.soundguys.com/jlab-jbuds-lux-anc-review-114634/">JLab JBuds Lux ANC</a> prove it. At just $79.99 MSRP, they reduced approximately 80% of perceived outside noise in our testing, making them a great value for commuting, studying, or working in a busy office. Add a comfortable fit, USB-C audio, and app-based EQ, and you’ve got an affordable pair of headphones that covers the essentials.</p> </div><div class="e_e"><div class="e_y8"><div class="e_D8"><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>Battery life is another highlight. The JBuds Lux ANC lasted 44 hours and 22 minutes with ANC enabled in our testing, giving you plenty of listening time between charges.</p></div><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>We also appreciate the flexibility of USB-C audio, which lets you listen over a wired connection instead of Bluetooth. The companion app offers EQ adjustments, so you can customize the sound to your preferences.</p> </div><div class="e_e e_lf"><q>The JLab JBuds Lux ANC block out approximately 80% of perceived outside noise for just $79.99.</q></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <p>While their ANC can’t quite match the strongest performers on this list, the JBuds Lux ANC offer an excellent balance of performance, features, and price. They’re an easy recommendation if you want capable noise canceling headphones without spending more than $100.</p> </div><div class="e_rF e_f e_e e_c7"><button type="button" class="e_f7" aria-label="Play video"><span class="e_g7"></span></button></div></div></div><button type="button" class="e_C8 e_T1 e_31 e_Z1 e_V1">Read more</button></div></div><span class="e_C6"><div class="e_D6" id="id-5378-7142"></div></span><div class="e_e e_P5"><div class="e_e e_lf"><h2>EarFun Wave Pro: The best budget noise canceling headphones for travel</h2> </div><div class="e_G8"><div class="e_I8"></div><div class="e_M8"><a referrerPolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://clearbuy.com/redirect/70b421375929415c8cad6cbda1ae4fefdd26c01c?pId=5378&amp;tag=sgwaw18-20" class="e_N8">EarFun Wave Pro</a><div class="e_O8">ANC • Battery life • LDAC</div><div class="e_zO e_P8"><div class="e_AO"></div></div><div class="e_Q8">MSRP: $79.99</div><div class="e_R8">Wireless noise canceling headphones at a great price.</div><div class="e_S8">With great battery life, advanced Bluetooth connectivity, and noise canceling, the EarFun Wave Pro provides exceptional value at an affordable price.</div></div><div class="e_T8"><div class="e_U8"><a referrerPolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://clearbuy.com/redirect/70b421375929415c8cad6cbda1ae4fefdd26c01c?pId=5378&amp;tag=sgwaw18-20" class="e_T1 e_41 e_W1 e_V1">See price at Amazon</a><a referrerPolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://clearbuy.com/redirect/6b876d09ff9d0177092b7c24e54f6323ea22c289?pId=5378&amp;tag=sgwaw18-20" class="e_T1 e_41 e_Z1 e_V1">See price at Manufacturer site</a></div><div class="e_W8"><div class="e_X8">Positives</div><ul class="e_Y8"><li class="e__8">Comfort</li><li class="e__8">Companion app</li><li class="e__8">Bluetooth 5.3 with LDAC</li><li class="e__8">Battery Life</li><li class="e__8">ANC</li></ul></div><div class="e_V8"><div class="e_X8">Cons</div><ul class="e_Y8"><li class="e__8">No audio over USB</li><li class="e__8">No touch controls</li><li class="e__8">No water resistance</li><li class="e__8">No auto play/pause</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="e_CJ"><div class="e_aJ"><div class="e_hJ"><button type="button" class="e_Lcb e_Ocb" title="Overlay this card&#x27;s lab curves with your pair and up to two more cards"><span class="e_Qcb">Pin to compare</span><small class="e_Rcb">0 of 3</small></button><button type="button" class="e_iJ"><span>Measurements</span><small class="e_lJ"></small></button><button type="button" class="e_iJ" disabled=""><span>Owners</span><small class="e_lJ">none yet</small></button></div></div></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <hr/> <p>The <a href="https://www.soundguys.com/earfun-wave-pro-review-112748/">EarFun Wave Pro</a> are a great choice for frequent travelers who don’t want to spend a fortune on headphones. At $79.99, they reduced an average of 80% of outside noise in our testing, making them useful for reducing distractions during flights and commutes. They’re comfortable for extended listening sessions, fold up into an included carrying case, and lasted an impressive 52 hours and 31 minutes with ANC enabled in our battery test.</p> </div><div class="e_e"><div class="e_y8"><div class="e_D8"><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>We found the Wave Pro particularly practical for travel thanks to their comfortable ear cushions, physical controls, and protective carrying case. You also get Bluetooth multipoint for switching between devices, LDAC support, and a companion app with EQ adjustments and different noise canceling modes.</p></div><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>Battery life is another strength. We measured 52 hours and 31 minutes with ANC turned on, while EarFun advertises up to 80 hours with ANC disabled. That’s why you might see a higher battery figure on the product card than in our testing. The headphones also support a 3.5mm wired connection, although ANC and app-based EQ aren’t available when listening this way.</p> </div><div class="e_e e_lf"><q>With 80% average noise reduction, more than 52 hours of tested battery life, and an included carrying case, the EarFun Wave Pro are excellent travel headphones for under $80.</q></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <p>The Wave Pro aren’t without compromises. We found their sound acceptable for casual listening, but using the wired connection increases bass strength and reduces clarity. They also lack an IP rating and automatic play/pause detection. Still, for long flights, road trips, and daily commutes, they offer a lot of practical features for the money.</p> </div><div role="button" class="e_f"><div class="e_wqb"><div class="e_qub e_xqb"><div class="e_8O">Chase Bernath / SoundGuys</div></div><div class="e_4Bb e_lf">You can easily connect these headphones to iOS and Android devices alike.</div></div></div></div></div><button type="button" class="e_C8 e_T1 e_31 e_Z1 e_V1">Read more</button></div></div><span class="e_C6"><div class="e_D6" id="id-3847-7142"></div></span><div class="e_e e_P5"><div class="e_e e_lf"><h2>1MORE SonoFlow: The best budget noise canceling headphones for battery life</h2> </div><div class="e_G8"><div class="e_I8"></div><div class="e_M8"><a referrerPolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://clearbuy.com/redirect/b8a293ea247b740fb2d19a35bccccfd2f03614e6?pId=3847&amp;tag=sgwaw18-20" class="e_N8">1More SonoFlow</a><div class="e_O8">Comfortable fit and well-padded • In-app EQ • Long battery life</div><div class="e_zO e_P8"><div class="e_AO"></div></div><div class="e_Q8">MSRP: $99.99</div><div class="e_R8">Feature rich with a stylish design, the SonoFlow headphones are all about value</div><div class="e_S8">The 1MORE SonoFlow are good-sounding, feature-rich headphones that won&#x27;t break the bank. Commuters and travelers will enjoy the ANC, long battery life, and plush ear pads. Experienced listeners will enjoy decent sound and EQ options.</div></div><div class="e_T8"><div class="e_U8"><a referrerPolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://clearbuy.com/redirect/b8a293ea247b740fb2d19a35bccccfd2f03614e6?pId=3847&amp;tag=sgwaw18-20" class="e_T1 e_41 e_W1 e_V1">See price at Amazon</a></div><div class="e_W8"><div class="e_X8">Positives</div><ul class="e_Y8"><li class="e__8">Comfortable fit and well-padded</li><li class="e__8">In-app EQ</li><li class="e__8">Long battery life</li><li class="e__8">Stylish design</li><li class="e__8">Travel case included</li><li class="e__8">Attractive price</li></ul></div><div class="e_V8"><div class="e_X8">Cons</div><ul class="e_Y8"><li class="e__8">Headband heavy</li><li class="e__8">Low clamping force</li><li class="e__8">No continuous power or connection indicator</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <hr/> <p>If you hate constantly charging your headphones, the <a href="https://www.soundguys.com/1more-sonoflow-review-101165/">1MORE SonoFlow</a> are worth a look. They lasted an incredible 56 hours and 51 minutes with ANC enabled in our testing, beating every other pick on this list. At $99.99 MSRP, you also get comfortable ear cushions, a foldable design, and an included travel case. Our testing gave their noise canceling a score of 66%, so ANC isn’t their biggest strength, but the battery life makes them an excellent choice for anyone who prioritizes listening time between charges.</p> </div><div class="e_e"><div class="e_y8"><div class="e_D8"><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>We found the SonoFlow comfortable for extended listening thanks to their well-padded ear cups. Their ANC also helped reduce bus rumble and distractions from nearby appliances during everyday use. The headphones support LDAC, and the 1MORE Music app offers EQ presets and custom adjustments to help you find your preferred sound.</p></div><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>Battery life is where they really shine. Our 56-hour, 51-minute result actually exceeds 1MORE’s advertised 50 hours with ANC on. The company also claims a five-minute charge provides up to five hours of listening, which is handy when you forget to charge before heading out.</p> </div><div class="e_e e_lf"><q>The 1MORE SonoFlow lasted nearly 57 hours with ANC enabled in our testing, making them our battery-life champions under $150.</q></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <p>There are a few compromises. We found the headband somewhat heavy, and the relatively low clamping force may not suit everyone. There’s also no IP rating, and ANC doesn’t work when you use the included wired audio cable. Still, if your biggest priority is going as long as possible between charges, the SonoFlow are hard to beat for the price.</p> </div><div role="button" class="e_f"><div class="e_wqb"><div class="e_qub e_xqb"></div><div class="e_4Bb e_lf">The original 1MORE SonoFlow headphones offer wired mode, a carrying case, and Hi-Res audio.</div></div></div></div></div><button type="button" class="e_C8 e_T1 e_31 e_Z1 e_V1">Read more</button></div></div><span class="e_C6"><div class="e_D6" id="id-6602-7142"></div></span><div class="e_e e_P5"><div class="e_e e_lf"><h2>OneOdio Focus A6: The best future proof budget noise canceling headphones</h2> </div><div class="e_G8"><div class="e_I8"></div><div class="e_M8"><a referrerPolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://clearbuy.com/redirect/eee1a93288f190bd4b530ad8e3f7fb8817442c9d?pId=6602&amp;tag=sgwaw18-20" class="e_N8">OneOdio Focus A6</a><div class="e_O8">Bluetooth 6.0 with LDAC • Battery life • ANC • Lightweight • Affordable price</div><div class="e_Q8">MSRP: $69.99</div><div class="e_R8">Future-ready headphones at an affordable price.</div><div class="e_S8">Get a 15% discount with code: SOUNDGUYS</div></div><div class="e_T8"><div class="e_U8"><a referrerPolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://clearbuy.com/redirect/eee1a93288f190bd4b530ad8e3f7fb8817442c9d?pId=6602&amp;tag=sgwaw18-20" class="e_T1 e_41 e_W1 e_V1">See price at Amazon</a><a referrerPolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://clearbuy.com/redirect/00c28244316dc4b12ddb0ecf554b2f3317147cb5?pId=6602&amp;tag=sgwaw18-20" class="e_T1 e_41 e_Z1 e_V1">See price at Manufacturer site</a></div><div class="e_W8"><div class="e_X8">Positives</div><ul class="e_Y8"><li class="e__8">Bluetooth 6.0 with LDAC</li><li class="e__8">Battery life</li><li class="e__8">ANC</li><li class="e__8">Lightweight</li><li class="e__8">Affordable price</li></ul></div><div class="e_V8"><div class="e_X8">Cons</div><ul class="e_Y8"><li class="e__8">No wired playback</li><li class="e__8">No travel case</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="e_CJ"><div class="e_aJ"><div class="e_hJ"><button type="button" class="e_Lcb e_Ocb" title="Overlay this card&#x27;s lab curves with your pair and up to two more cards"><span class="e_Qcb">Pin to compare</span><small class="e_Rcb">0 of 3</small></button><button type="button" class="e_iJ"><span>Measurements</span><small class="e_lJ"></small></button><button type="button" class="e_iJ" disabled=""><span>Owners</span><small class="e_lJ">none yet</small></button></div></div></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <hr/> <p>The <a href="https://www.soundguys.com/1more-sonoflow-review-101165/">OneOdio Focus A6</a> pack an impressive amount of technology into headphones costing just $69.99. They were the first Bluetooth 6.0 headphones we tested, and they also support LDAC, Bluetooth multipoint, and a customizable companion app. In our testing, they reduced an average of 79% of outside noise, which is impressive at this price. We also found them lightweight and comfortable enough for everyday listening, making them a great option if you want modern features without spending much.</p> </div><div class="e_e"><div class="e_y8"><div class="e_D8"><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>Bluetooth 6.0 is the headline feature, although its potential benefits aren’t all available yet. For example, the standard supports more precise device location tracking, but OneOdio hasn’t implemented that feature in its app. What you can use right now is LDAC for compatible Android devices, multipoint connectivity, and a seven-band EQ for adjusting the sound.</p></div><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>We found the Focus A6 comfortable during travel thanks to their lightweight 240g design and memory foam ear cushions. The companion app is another highlight, offering multiple ANC modes, a Find My Headphones feature, and useful extras like a volume limiter. The sound has some extra bass strength and reduced midrange presence, but you can make adjustments using the EQ.</p> </div><div class="e_e e_lf"><q>With Bluetooth 6.0, LDAC, and 79% average noise reduction, the OneOdio Focus A6 offer an impressive feature set for just $69.99.</q></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <p>OneOdio advertises up to 40 hours of battery life with ANC enabled, or 75 hours with it off, although our battery testing is still ongoing. The plastic construction can creak, and there’s no carrying case or wired playback option. Still, if connectivity and customization matter most to you, the Focus A6 offer plenty for the money.</p> </div><div role="button" class="e_f"><div class="e_wqb"><div class="e_qub e_xqb"><div class="e_8O">Chase Bernath / SoundGuys</div></div><div class="e_4Bb e_lf">The OneOdio Focus A6 come in a Midnight Black or Ivory Blush color option.</div></div></div></div></div><button type="button" class="e_C8 e_T1 e_31 e_Z1 e_V1">Read more</button></div></div><span class="e_C6"><div class="e_D6" id="id-6789-7142"></div></span><div class="e_e e_lf"> <h2>CMF Headphone Pro: The best budget noise canceling headphones for customization</h2> </div><div class="e_G8"><div class="e_I8"></div><div class="e_M8"><a href="https://dealhunt.co/us-B0FKG6TDRR" class="e_N8">CMF Headphone Pro</a><div class="e_O8">Battery life • ANC • LDAC</div><div class="e_zO e_P8"><div class="e_AO"></div></div><div class="e_Q8">MSRP: $99.00</div><div class="e_R8">Bass-heavy budget wireless headphones.</div><div class="e_S8">Budget headphones that deliver strong battery life and ANC, with LDAC support, and spatial audio.</div></div><div class="e_T8"><div class="e_U8"><a href="https://dealhunt.co/us-B0FKG6TDRR" class="e_T1 e_41 e_W1 e_V1">$49.00 at Amazon</a></div><div class="e_W8"><div class="e_X8">Positives</div><ul class="e_Y8"><li class="e__8">Battery life</li><li class="e__8">ANC</li><li class="e__8">LDAC</li></ul></div><div class="e_V8"><div class="e_X8">Cons</div><ul class="e_Y8"><li class="e__8">Build quality</li><li class="e__8">Limited EQ</li><li class="e__8">Bass slider doesn&#x27;t improve sound</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="e_CJ"><div class="e_aJ"><div class="e_hJ"><button type="button" class="e_Lcb e_Ocb" title="Overlay this card&#x27;s lab curves with your pair and up to two more cards"><span class="e_Qcb">Pin to compare</span><small class="e_Rcb">0 of 3</small></button><button type="button" class="e_iJ"><span>Measurements</span><small class="e_lJ"></small></button><button type="button" class="e_iJ"><span>Owners</span><small class="e_lJ">4 reviews</small></button></div></div><div hidden=""><section class="e_0cb" aria-label="Owners of the CMF BY NOTHING Headphone Pro"><header class="e_1cb"><p class="e_2cb"><span class="e_3cb">From owners</span><span class="e_4cb">4 owner reviews · 4 of 4 would buy again · 1 photo-verified · owners report ~85 h per charge vs 100 h claimed</span></p><a class="e_5cb" href="/community/products/cmf-by-nothing-headphone-pro/">All 4 →</a></header><div class="e_6cb e_Sj"><article class="e_Ji e_0i"><div class="e_Ni"><p class="e_Si"><span class="e_Xi"><span class="e_7V"><span class="e_I e_K e_Q" role="img" aria-label="Contributor tier">H</span><a class="e_Ui" href="/community/members/hackneyedlisten87/">hackneyedlisten87</a></span><span class="e_mT">⁠<button type="button" class="e_nT e_pT" aria-label="Signed-in owner"></button><span id=":R92ja8m7r6d6:" role="tooltip" hidden="" class="e_sT e_t