s="e_jib"></div></div></div></article><article class="e_Ji e_0i"><div class="e_Ni"><p class="e_Si"><span class="e_Xi"><span class="e_7V"><span class="e_I e_K e_Q" role="img" aria-label="Contributor tier">DE</span><a class="e_Ui" href="/community/members/deep_elm_96/">deep_elm_96</a></span><span class="e_mT">⁠<button type="button" class="e_nT e_pT" aria-label="Signed-in owner"></button><span id=":R92na8m7r6d6:" role="tooltip" hidden="" class="e_sT e_tT"><b class="e_uT">Signed-in owner.</b> This member signed in to publish, so their reviews count for points and show on their profile.</span></span></span><span class="e_V e_Wj">Owner · 1–6 months</span><span class="e_cj e_dj"><span>↻ </span>Would buy again</span><time class="e_Yi" dateTime="2026-09-28T12:58:49.989Z">· Sep 2026</time></p><blockquote class="e_Zi e__i"><a class="e_1i" href="/community/products/cmf-by-nothing-headphone-pro/107ffbf9-9cb3-427a-baf7-a372274af312/">“For me, the bass is too low from the default eq so it needs a little bit of fine tuning before using it. Other than that battery life is astonishing it somehow lasts nearly 2 weeks with me using it every day at the subway and at home while studying.”</a></blockquote><ul class="e_8i"><li class="e_9i e_aj"><span class="e_-i">✓</span><span class="e_Dj">Better than expected: </span>Noise cancelling in the real world</li><li class="e_9i e_aj"><span class="e_-i">✓</span><span class="e_Dj">Better than expected: </span>Battery in real life</li><li class="e_9i e_aj"><span class="e_-i">✓</span><span class="e_Dj">Better than expected: </span>Fit and build after months</li></ul><div class="e_lib e_qj"><span id=":R1rna8m7r6d6:" class="e_mib">Did this help you decide?</span><span class="e_nib" role="group" aria-labelledby=":R1rna8m7r6d6:"><button type="button" class="e_oib">Yes</button><button type="button" class="e_oib">No</button></span><span class="e_rib">Be the first to say</span><div class="e_vib"></div><button type="button" class="e_5hb">Ask deep_elm_96</button></div><div id=":Rbna8m7r6d6:" class="e_9hb e_Vj" hidden=""><ul class="e_-hb"><li><button type="button" class="e_6hb">Still using them every day?</button></li><li><button type="button" class="e_6hb">Comfortable with glasses on?</button></li><li><button type="button" class="e_6hb">How do you sound to people on calls?</button></li></ul><div class="e_jib"></div></div></div></article></div></section></div></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <hr/> <p>The <a href="https://www.soundguys.com/cmf-headphone-pro-review-a-solid-b-side-146595/">CMF Headphone Pro </a>stand out from other budget noise canceling headphones thanks to their customizable design. For $99, you get swappable ear cushions in different colors, physical controls, and a companion app that lets you personalize your listening experience. Our testing shows they reduce an average of 81% of outside noise, while their 43 hours and 9 minutes of battery life with ANC enabled means you won’t be reaching for the charger very often. Add LDAC support and Bluetooth multipoint, and there’s plenty to like for the price.</p> </div><div class="e_e"><div class="e_y8"><div class="e_D8"><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>The swappable ear cushions are the main attraction here. You can mix and match colors to give the headphones a different look, although additional cushions cost $25 per pair. We also appreciate the personal sound profiling feature in the Nothing X app, which adjusts the sound based on a short hearing test.</p></div><div class="e_e e_lf"><p>There are a few other ways to customize the experience, including a three-band EQ and an Energy Slider that adjusts bass or treble strength. However, we found the slider more gimmicky than useful, since increasing the bass strength can make music sound boomy. The small, closely spaced controls also take some getting used to.</p> </div><div class="e_e e_lf"><q>With swappable ear cushions, 81% average noise reduction, and more than 43 hours of tested battery life, the CMF Headphone Pro offer plenty of personality for $99.</q></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <p>The biggest compromises are the plastic construction and comfort over longer sessions. We noticed some creaking in the build, and the headband can become uncomfortable after extended listening. The headphones also don’t fold, making them less convenient for travel than the EarFun Wave Pro. Still, if you want affordable ANC headphones that you can personalize, the CMF Headphone Pro are worth considering.</p> </div><div class="e_rF e_f e_e e_c7"><button type="button" class="e_f7" aria-label="Play video"><span class="e_g7"></span></button></div></div></div><button type="button" class="e_C8 e_T1 e_31 e_Z1 e_V1">Read more</button></div><hr class="e_e e_U6"/><span class="e_C6"><div class="e_D6" id="id-honorable-mentions-7142"></div></span><div class="e_e e_lf"> <h2>Honorable mentions</h2> </div><div class="e_Zrb e_g5 e_h5 e_e"><a id="deal-7" class="e_k">Edifier W830NB</a><div class="e__rb"></div><div class="e_-rb"></div><a href="https://dealhunt.co/us-B0D2VH915C" class="e_1rb">Edifier W830NB</a><div class="e_2rb">Price • ANC • Sound quality</div><div class="e_3rb"><div class="e_zO e_8rb"><div class="e_AO"></div></div><span class="e_9rb">MSRP: $79.99</span><div class="e_WE e_7rb e_YE"></div></div><div class="e_4rb">A budget-friendly cans with a solid feature-set.</div><div class="e_5rb">The Edifier W830NB headphones are ready to take on your daily commute.</div><div class="e_6rb"><div class="e_1pb e_2pb"><div class="e_5pb"><a href="https://dealhunt.co/us-B0D2VH915C" class="e_Q9 e_lcb e_3pb" title="$79.99 at Amazon"><div class="e_R9"><span class="e_S9">$79.99 at Amazon</span></div></a></div><div class="e_dqb"><div class="e_kqb e_Zwb"><div class="e_lqb"></div></div></div></div></div><div class="e_dsb"><div class="e_XJ e_CJ"><div class="e_aJ"><div class="e_hJ"><button type="button" class="e_Lcb e_Ocb" title="Overlay this card&#x27;s lab curves with your pair and up to two more cards"><span class="e_Qcb">Pin to compare</span><small class="e_Rcb">0 of 3</small></button><button type="button" class="e_iJ"><span>Measurements</span><small class="e_lJ"></small></button><button type="button" class="e_iJ" disabled=""><span>Owners</span><small class="e_lJ">none yet</small></button></div></div></div></div></div><div></div><div class="e_e e_lf"> <p><strong><a href="https://www.soundguys.com/edifier-w830nb-review-131499/">Edifier W830NB</a>:</strong> The W830NB are a strong alternative to the JLab JBuds Lux ANC, particularly if you want more control over your sound. Our testing shows they reduce an average of 76% of outside noise, and we liked their comfortable fit, LDAC support, USB-C audio, and excellent four-band parametric EQ. The biggest drawbacks are the lack of a carrying case and plastic that scratches easily.</p> <hr/> </div><div class="e_Zrb e_g5 e_h5 e_e"><a id="deal-8" class="e_k">Sony ULT WEAR</a><div class="e__rb"></div><div class="e_-rb"></div><a href="https://dealhunt.co/us-B0CWVXTK6Z" class="e_1rb">Sony ULT WEAR</a><div class="e_2rb">Comfortable • Long battery life • Immersive sound</div><div class="e_3rb"><div class="e_zO e_8rb"><div class="e_AO"></div></div><span class="e_9rb">MSRP: $229.99</span><div class="e_WE e_7rb e_YE"></div></div><div class="e_4rb">Press ULT to rattle skull</div><div class="e_5rb">The Sony ULT WEAR headphones are a new generation of folding, wireless headphones with ANC and a big, comfy design. Good connectivity options and a focus on immersive sound are the key selling features.</div><div class="e_6rb"><div class="e_1pb e_2pb"><div class="e_5pb"><a href="https://dealhunt.co/us-B0CWVXTK6Z" class="e_Q9 e_lcb e_3pb" title="$148.00 at Amazon"><div class="e_R9"><span class="e_S9">$148.00 at Amazon</span></div></a></div><div class="e_dqb"><div class="e_kqb e_Zwb"><div class="e_lqb"></div></div></div></div></div><div class="e_dsb"><div class="e_XJ e_CJ"><div class="e_aJ"><div class="e_hJ"><button type="button" class="e_Lcb e_Ocb" title="Overlay t